# Map Files

Never modify any Dungeon Master map file.

This includes all map JSON files (for example `Assets/Data/Maps/**`) and any other files containing dungeon/map tile data.

## Allowed

- Read/inspect map files
- Search map files
- Report map coordinates, tile types, or problems
- Suggest exactly what the user should change manually
- Modify Unity editor/tools that help edit maps through Unity, if the user explicitly requests it

## Not allowed

- Edit map files directly
- Rewrite map JSON
- Change tile coordinates
- Change tile types/content
- Automatically fix map data
- Generate and overwrite corrected map files

All map-data changes must be performed by the user manually or through Unity.

Viewport/editor assets such as `ViewportLayout.asset` and `ViewportPoseVisibility.asset` are not map files and are not covered by this restriction.
